Z||000000||FieroTig||05-04-2001||04:46 PM||||i am having a wierd problem with my cvar and was wondering if anyone knew how to help.<BR>i have an 85 GT auto... the car starts and runs nice. pretty fast 2 for an auto, but when i drive it for more than like 20 minutes the tach starts to bounce, even though the engine sounds like it isn't, after about 5 minutes it gets to the point where it bounces past the governer and kills the car. then i have to stop the car, wait about five minutes so i can drive on, then 15 minutes later it will do the same thing, stop the car again, wait five minurtes, then drive on... and it continues this forever.. any ideas? please help!!!!||||reg||4
Z||000001||mrfixit58||05-04-2001||05:17 PM||||First off, welcome to the forum. You'll find a LOT of useful information and help here. <P>Second, sounds like you've got a bad tach filter. They are not available from GM any longer but Rodney Dickman sells a good replacement: <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/</A> <P>Third, the search function on the forum works really well. I encourage you to give it a try. Not that we still won't answer any question you may have, but you may find your answer faster if you don't have to wait on someone to respond. <P>Again, welcome,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||FieroTig||05-04-2001||05:52 PM||||hey thanks.. i have 3 fiero's and have been looking for a good forum to join. looks like i found one. i will try that, and thanks for welcoming me!||||reg||6
Z||000003||Bob Englert||05-04-2001||06:37 PM||||I had a similar problem with my blue 87 GT.<P>The tach started jumping around and the car died 3 times while trying to get it home.  I did a COMPLETE tuneup (new distributor, module, coil, cap, rotor, plugs, wires). and it ran great for about 10 days and started acting up again.<P>What I saw was it would be OK until I got the RPM's over about 2500, then it would start missing and bouncing.  I ordered Rodney's tach filter and the car has been solid ever since.<P>I wanted to do a complete tune up anyway!<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
